ustry  and i'm gonna try and not get too far  into the weeds on this but  typical issues involve things like what  is called crunch  crunch times where you know we got we  need all hands on deck sort of thing  which have a tendency to mean that  people are working  up to 80 or sometimes even 100 hour  weeks  are not getting paid proper overtime for  doing so  even though no one deliberately says you  need to work these extra hours or you  will get fired  it is still understood that if they are  not putting in as many extra hours as  their co-workers that they are liable to  be replaced  this is a very damaging and  harmful culture for a lot of people on  the lower end of the totem pole  within that industry and when that gets  called out  or in even more egregious examples a  company like  ubisoft which has  high end executives who horrible  horrible things about their treatment of  their employees are coming out  there are people who say fans  who say well we still have to buy the  games because we have to support the  developers the people who made it  saying that we can't abandon this  because it'll hurt the victims you're  not  saving them you're perpetuating the  workplace because you are rewarding  the company that is working them to  death  and that's one of the weird nuances that  is really hard to parse  with something like buffy where i'm  fairly secure in saying that a lot of  the stars  get some form of residual checks  every time it is aired on television or  picked up for a new streaming service or  there's a new  uh home video release or what have you  so they do get something  from that but unless you know  everybody's contract  unless you know who's gonna benefit and  who isn't  then i i'm very antsy about hearing that  kind of defense deployed  in situations like joss whedon and i can  certainly tell you that none of the  ground level people  you know the the grips the camera people  set dressers makeup  none of them are getting residuals the  only people are going to get residuals  are going to be people like the headline  stars  and i don't want to go so far as to  suggest that  claims to defend them and their works  and their residual  checks are being made in bad faith i  don't want to go so far as to say that  anyone who says that is just deploying  it as an excuse to not give up something  that they like  that can and does happen but i don't  believe that everyone who says that sort  of thing  is that way i i honestly do not i've  seen some very good very passionate  defenses of this perspective from people  who  i admire and respect and believe that  they are honest in their position  and they are and i also believe that  they are introspective enough to  have considered the sorts of things that  i'm talking about  but again my concern is  this idea of well we can't  cancel something because of the  collateral damage  because this is the thing that came up  in  both the joss whedon and the gina carano  video  ultimately it's about money  the reason these people are being  removed  from the positions and the work that  they were doing  or may have trouble finding work in the  future  is not because of a moral stance and i'm  not saying fans aren't taking one they  are  but i'm saying the people who actually  write the paychecks who decide whether  or not these  individuals are employed who decide  whether or not to hire them in future  they only care about the  money  and ultimately if  they go through the calculations  of well okay this person's controversial  this problem has happened with them in  the past but  hey people are still buying their  product and i'm not saying that's going  to happen with joss whedon  i'm not saying if you keep watching  buffy the vampire slayer on whatever  streaming service is currently on  that suddenly he's gonna be allowed to  run a film set again and be abusive  towards actors again i i am not saying  that  do not twist me on that  however that general mentality  of as long as the money is coming  in is at the root of why  whedon was in a position of power  for as long as he was  and i cannot help but feel that  making a defense of  we can't cancel it it sounds like  talking about the banks too big to fail  okay but if you're going to continue to  prop it up you have to be very careful  about how you do it  because if you just say well we can't  let this sink and disappear and vanish  but don't do the introspective and put  the caveats and put the asterisk  next to joss whedon's name that needs to  be there  forever then it doesn't incentivize  these situations getting better  it continues to perpetuate the kind of  environment  where these people will continue to be  protected which is a huge part  of what i found very powerful about  charisma carpenter's statement  about joss whedon the specifics that she  cited  were terrible but it troubles me that  people got very  fixated on those specifics  and seemed to gloss over the fact that  she pointed out  as did ray fisher before her  that he was protected  coddled and rewarded by the people who  had the ability to stop  him and the only thing those people care  about is money  and allowing these things could to  continue to be profitable  you run the risk of perpetuating that  system and those people and that  mentality  again i say run the risk i'm not saying  you are doing that  you you right there who haven't gotten  rid of every single piece of buffy  paraphernalia that you have this is your  no i am  not and will not say that  but i'm saying be careful  because you may make the assessment  of something like buffy the vampire  slayer or firefly or  angel or dollhouse and come to the  conclusion  this still matters enough to me that i  wish to continue to engage with it  i wish to continue to talk about it i  wish to continue  to be part of the fandom that still  exists around it  that is fine be careful  about letting that become your default  mentality  every time something like this happens  these things need to be addressed on a  case-by-case basis because  no two instances are ever identical  so look inside yourself  consider the damage of  cancelling something like buffy  consider the damage of  leaving it as is consider those things  look inside yourself make your call  do your best to not judge other people  for theirs unless they're being  jerks you know if someone's being or  whatever but  come to your conclusion try to be fair  to people who might come to a different  one  than you do but also be  careful about letting that thought  process having gone through it once  just become a template that you apply to  each  other instance that this happens because  i said before this is going to keep  happening  be prepared to do the work that's  another thing i've said before  processing on this stuff sucks  it really really  sucks and doing the work  is never fun but that is always what i'm  going to push for  that is why i don't tell you what to do  or what to think  i try to the best of my ability to give  you things to take into account  so that when this video is over you can  consider  for yourself the things that i've said  the information and the knowledge and  the feelings that you already had  and process it and think about it  and not just default to an answer  because that answer applied in a  previous situation  so i think that's going to be it now  this is not a sponsored video however  i would like to shout out hi ho  silverworks  you'll find a link down in the  description they made this  uh particular design uh and  i actually have a number of their  designs i love this hoodie this was my  first crop top hoodie  something i never had before and like i  kind of love it  they have wonderful things they're a  terrific  artist with wonderful designs available  on their site i would encourage you to  check them out  and you can also find them on tick tock  for some fun content there as well  i should probably plug the patreon which  is how i cover my bills  and is what keeps this entire thing up  and running  even if you're not able to do that like  share subscribe they all help me out  this stuff sucks when it happens  but i want you to remember  you are beautiful you are valid  and you are loved you are the council  i am just running the meetings and until  next time hopefully on a more enjoyable  topic  this council is adjourned  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

